      "text": [
        ": سَأَلْتُهُ عَنِ اَلرَّجُلِ يُقَصِّرُ فِي ضَيْعَتِهِ فَقَالَ «لاَ بَأْسَ مَا لَمْ يَنْوِ مُقَامَ عَشَرَةِ أَيَّامٍ إِلاَّ أَنْ يَكُونَ لَهُ بِهَا مَنْزِلٌ يَسْتَوْطِنُهُ» قَالَ قُلْتُ لَهُ مَا اَلاِسْتِيطَانُ فَقَالَ «أَنْ يَكُونَ لَهُ بِهَا مَنْزِلٌ يُقِيمُ فِيهِ سِتَّةَ أَشْهُرٍ فَإِذَا كَانَ كَذَلِكَ يُتِمُّ فِيهَا مَتَى دَخَلَهَا."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.bab-ul-qaim-publications": [
          "Hadith.1308 - Muhammad ibn Isma'il ibn Bazi' reported from Abu al-Hasan al-Ridha (as) that he asked about a man shortening his prayers at his property.\nImam (as) said: \"There is no harm as long as he does not intend to stay for ten days, unless he has a house there where he resides.\"\nI asked him, \"What is meant by 'resides'?\"\nImam (as) said: \"It means he has a house where he stays for six months. If that is the case, he should complete (his prayers) whenever he enters it.\""
        ]
      }
